Upstream-Status: Pending

6.1 turned FS-Cache on by itself. In 6.18 the option depends on
NETFS_SUPPORT, which has no prompt and is selected only by a network
filesystem. Select it from FS-Cache so cachefiles still builds.

--- a/fs/netfs/Kconfig
+++ b/fs/netfs/Kconfig
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ config NETFS_DEBUG
 
 config FSCACHE
 	bool "General filesystem local caching manager"
-	depends on NETFS_SUPPORT
+	select NETFS_SUPPORT
 	help
 	  This option enables a generic filesystem caching manager that can be
 	  used by various network and other filesystems to cache data locally.
